# TJS-2504 cryptography consultation

2026-10-19. Responds to Core comment `a24e38fc-580d-4fea-89de-ac616eadd346` and the writer's follow-up `fb58a037-4cf6-47d2-8870-9c0e7f1c272a` on [TJS-2504](/TJS/issues/TJS-2504).

**Ruling: accept both directions for bounded non-public implementation.** Use a dedicated TESTNET, v1 genesis and v18 from height one, with version-one cutoff zero. Use a v1 genesis block containing a native-serialized v2/RCTNull coinbase, one height-zero generation input, unlock time 60 and one amount-zero `txout_to_key`, with publicly reproducible native-derived subgroup-valid keys. Preserve upstream FCMP++/CARROT, spend authorization, commitments, proof verification and torsion checks.

This completes the requested consultation. The writer may implement and produce the exact candidate within the existing task authority. No further conceptual genesis/activation ruling is pending from me. **Absent genesis bytes and the final launch candidate remain unaccepted, with insufficient native evidence.** A failed required check requires correcting the candidate and independent review, never a validation exception.

## Exact object reviewed

State family: source-reviewed protocol proposal, not a compiled or running final-profile network. Candidate `4d89b4a35d0a3c8d8f40648989d5b6ffacc2e7b7`, unchanged assigned task branch. Canonical profile SHA256 `b1711b3114e234a4975bcefc6f02fa1175df1d213ed03372bb5c50bc503aef31`. Source-lock SHA256 `f70160e8b7de56bfaed50ed6d29155ea0fcb41789f0c2cfcd15019085c82d001`. Upstream is [seraphis-migration/monero at e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/tree/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2). Existing crypto pins and settled monetary policy are unchanged.

`source-review.json` binds 25 inspected native files to both working bytes and the pinned Git objects. Ten decisive files also match bytes fetched from the public raw-source URLs recorded there. Cargo.lock and five submodule HEADs pass the existing source checker. This is not full-tree or executable provenance; the cache retains the disclosed test CMake injection. No repository file or native source was changed during this consultation.

## Assurance basis and required clarification

| Boundary | Source observation and ruling |
| --- | --- |
| Mandatory intended crypto | At [blockchain.cpp:3482-3505](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_core/blockchain.cpp#L3482-L3505), v17 allows FCMP++ while v18 requires it for ordinary transactions. Lines 3681-3703 reject nonempty legacy rings only above v17. [Output checking](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_basic/cryptonote_format_utils.cpp#L1313-L1335) requires CARROT above v17. Accept the v18 direction and reject permanent v17. |
| Skipped activation versions | [Earliest-height lookup](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_basic/hardfork.cpp#L383-L393) uses `>=`, so asking for the v17 threshold resolves to height one in the proposed v18 table. [Regtest](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_core.cpp#L655-L661) supplies a structural precedent, not TESTNET proof. Test the actual fork state and wallet together. |
| Genesis format and torsion | [Miner prevalidation](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_core/blockchain.cpp#L1401-L1432) supports the proposed height/unlock/output structure. The output is legacy only at the v1 genesis. At lines 1512-1537, TESTNET does not receive FAKECHAIN's genesis exemption. Unlock60 reaches the height-one FCMP++ threshold, so the nonempty-output and torsion checks apply even to genesis. |
| Native key derivation | [crypto.cpp:198-279](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/crypto/crypto.cpp#L198-L279) supplies deterministic recovery, scalar-to-public-key and existing output-key derivation. Publish all recipe inputs and use nonzero canonical scalars and nonidentity subgroup points. `check_key` only establishes curve decoding; it is not subgroup assurance. Native torsion checking must pass for the final output and commitment. Publicly known genesis key material is acceptable only because its output carries zero value; this does not establish that the output is unspendable. |
| Amount-zero commitment | [The native amount collector](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_core/tx_verification_utils.cpp#L491-L531) includes zero. `get_commitment` uses that map for coinbase. [zeroCommitVartime](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/ringct/rctOps.cpp#L47-L50) has an amount-zero entry equal to encoded basepoint G, `58` followed by 31 `66` bytes. It represents the native unit-mask commitment G + 0H, not the identity or a zero-filled key. The commitment is derived rather than an extra serialized RCTNull output field. |
| Tree conversion | [Database insertion](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/blockchain_db/blockchain_db.cpp#L224-L239) stores the native commitment for v2 coinbase outputs. [Legacy leaf conversion](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/fcmp_pp/curve_trees.cpp#L89-L129) uses the original output key for the key-image generator and the existing torsion treatment. Preserve those rules. Check unlock scheduling and roots through maturity; do not assume a nonempty usable root immediately at height zero. |

Two implementation details must be explicit in the writer's overlay:

1. The ordinary [miner constructor](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_core/cryptonote_tx_utils.cpp#L146-L225) is not a ready-made genesis generator. Its amount decomposition [returns immediately for zero](https://github.com/seraphis-migration/monero/blob/e151643c5269c83bf24a83b2548e2493876026b2/src/cryptonote_basic/cryptonote_format_utils.h#L259-L264), producing no output; under v1 it also selects transaction version one. Construct the specified one-zero-output v2 transaction using existing native structures, derivation and serialization. Do not alter general decomposition to emit zero outputs everywhere.
2. Upstream reward validation requires the exact normal reward at v1. The zero-genesis policy needs an explicit height-zero construction/validation rule in the minimal selected-policy overlay. `already_generated_coins == 0` also holds before height one and cannot identify genesis. Preserve ordinary exact-coinbase, fee, penalty, overflow and generated-coins protections. No cryptographic verifier delta is approved by this ruling.

## Evidence required before accepting exact bytes

| Required native check | Observable acceptance condition |
| --- | --- |
| Serialization and identity | Reproduce the public recipe, serialize and parse through native code, roundtrip exact bytes, and pin transaction hash, full block/hash, actual nonce and recipe/source/build digests. Verify v1 block, v2/RCTNull coinbase, input height0, unlock60, exactly one amount0 output and valid output/extra public keys. No candidate blob or hash exists yet. |
| Genuine TESTNET admission and accounting | Fresh native TESTNET LMDB admits that exact genesis without test-options/FAKECHAIN substitution. Record zero generated coins and no allocation. Height one receives the ordinary selected reward. Reject a positive genesis reward, wrong height/unlock, empty outputs and invalid coinbase form through the relevant native paths. |
| Commitment, leaf and trusted root | Record the amount0 map entry, persisted native commitment, derived output pair/leaf and scheduled tree metadata. Record the root/depth actually required at height one and around genesis/funding-output maturity. Reopen the database and compare roots and accounting on two peers. Never add a fictional commitment field to the RCTNull wire format for a negative test. |
| Unchanged rejection rules | Admit the valid subgroup output; independently reject a validly encoded torsion-bearing output, identity/small-order output and malformed output. Exercise the native commitment/torsion helper with identity/torsion controls as appropriate, distinguish helper from block-admission results, and preserve failed diagnostics. Do not clear a bad new output and accept it as a replacement, copy historical torsion-bearing genesis keys, remove outputs, or add a genesis exemption. |
| Activation, proofs and value integrity | Record native fork state and wallet agreement at heights0/1 and after reopening. Admit a real FCMP++/CARROT transaction under v18; reject legacy proof/output/ring variants, invalid spend authorization, corrupt membership/range proof, balance/fee mutation and duplicate spend with checks attributable to the intended rule. Reuse unchanged proof fixtures where their premises still hold. |
| Funded wallet continuity | Mine mature non-genesis funding, send across final-profile nodes, receive, restore/rescan and perform a genuine subsequent spend. Pin transaction IDs, native admission, exact balances/fees and both nodes' tip/root state. Spending a public zero-valued genesis output cannot substitute for this test. Preserve private authenticated/restricted RPC. |

These are acceptance blockers if absent, not findings that the unimplemented candidate already fails. The required candidate still needs native separation, persistence/recovery, selected-policy/difficulty/capacity evidence and independent Core/Security review. Historical selected-policy and accepted upstream-regtest receipts keep their original scope. A deterministic zero-value genesis does not establish a large anonymity set or network-layer unlinkability; no production-readiness or audit claim follows.

## Handoff and disposition

Consultation complete. The existing P2P/Mining writer `3730ad68-e373-4c8a-84df-2e11327b86a5` owns applying this ruling in its profile/launch sheet, coordinating the bounded build slot with the platform owner, and producing the exact native vectors above on this same deliverable. Keep `launch_ready:false` until the real acceptance gates close. The existing issue remains a blocked, changes-requested launch deliverable with that named unblock owner/action; this consultation does not advance Core's review stage or take assignment from the writer.

Verified in this run: pinned source check, 25 working-file/Git-object matches, ten public-source matches, unchanged hashes for two retained accepted native receipts, clean unchanged candidate checkout, and readiness still refusing with exit3. No native build, node, container, endpoint, key custody or signing operation ran. The supplied scratch environment variables were absent; evidence uses this bridge run's private `scratch/cryptography-consultation` directory. Upload the evidence before run cleanup.

Needs TJ: None.

